## Corpus quality-max RE-RUN: triage grading bugs (2026-06-10 session 2, commit b05282e)

Re-ran .claude/workflows/quality-max.js (the engineering-DNA fan-out workflow built session 1, commit 2c3bede) against current state. wf_86bc4fa7-fbf: 17 agents, 8 confirmed / 2 refuted. The re-run surfaced triage-live.js grading bugs that BOTH the 7 manual sweeps AND the first workflow run missed (those focused on tutor/theme/SDK; the triage grading path was never deeply reviewed).

REAL BUGS FIXED (browser-witnessed via window.__triage on triage-live.html):
1. HIGH triage-live.js highlight_card: was `for(const c of state.cards) c.highlighted=(c.id===id)` (single-select). The grading SYS prompt calls highlight_card ONCE PER correct atom, so single-select left only the LAST highlighted -> hits capped at 1 -> score=100*1/atomCount (a 5/5 scored 20%). FIX: accumulate (find card, set highlighted=true). browser-704: 3 calls -> ['a','b','c'] accumulates:true. ALSO reset highlights on entry to a fresh grading turn (prev!=='grading') so re-grade starts clean.
2. MED triage-live.js set_phase graded branch: persistActive() ran at L601 BEFORE score computed at L607-608, so persistActive wrote `score: state.lastGrade ?? prevScore ?? null` = null; saveSessions() at L615 only serializes state.sessions, never re-derives. Grade lived only in transient state.lastGrade -> lost on reload (sessionScore->null->phase resets to 'asking'). FIX: added persistActive() AFTER state.lastGrade=score.
3. LOW triage-live.js buildSnapshot: SYSTEM_PROMPT_TMPL filled via string-pattern .replace('{{CARDS}}',cardsText) — JS String.replace special-cases $&/$'/$1 in the REPLACEMENT string. Card bodies are free LLM/user text ("give $500") -> mangled prompt. FIX: function replacements .replace('{{X}}',()=>val). browser-702 dollarSafe:true.
4. MED srs.js: removed 2 dead exports getEligibleCards (zero callers, not in window.__srs) + getEligibleDueCards (zero callers, body duplicates getDueCards, ticksAll param unread).
5. MED scripts/build_data.js: flat-layout fallback `SUBJECTS = SYLLABUS.subjects || [...8 subjects...]` OMITTED paediatrics + paediatrics-neonatal (syllabus.js DEFAULT_SUBJECTS has all 10). build_data does NOT import syllabus.js despite syllabus.js header claiming it as a consumer — and it CANNOT, because build_data.js carries an intentional NUL byte (offset ~350) inside stableCardId's `${front}\0${source}` hash template; the Edit tool round-trips UTF-8 and would mangle the NUL, changing EVERY card id. FIX: byte-preserving Node patch (read latin1, string-replace the SUBJECTS array, writeFileSync latin1) to complete the fallback list. NEVER use the Edit/Write tool on build_data.js — use a byte-level Node patch.

test.js: 4 guardrails added (highlight accumulate via !single-select regex on liveSrc; score re-persist regex; build_data paediatrics in fallback; — note $-safe not separately asserted). 19 pass.

KEY LESSON: re-running quality-max after the codebase/scope shifts is worth it — a whole subsystem (triage grading) that prior sweeps skipped yielded a HIGH scoring bug. The workflow's adversarial-verify (skeptic defaults refuted) filtered 2 false positives cleanly.

SHARED-SPOOL: peer session committed its tutor slice (app.js/tutor-panel.js/tutor-store.js) concurrently; I committed only my 4 explicit files (triage-live.js srs.js build_data.js test.js), left .gm/prd.yml unstaged (shared spool state).
